    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Use the quadratic formula to solve for $x$, expressing your answers in exact form.\n\n$(x+2)(x^2-6x+7)=0$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-2,\\ 3\\pm\\sqrt2$",
      "worked": "By the null factor law, $x=-2$ or $x^2-6x+7=0$. For the quadratic:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(1)(7)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt8}2\\\\x&=3\\pm\\sqrt2\\end{aligned}$$\nHence $x=-2,\\ 3+\\sqrt2,\\ 3-\\sqrt2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
